course: dictionary
lesson: 3864
title: Fragment: a small broken piece
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A fragment is a small piece that has broken off something bigger. The word also works for a small part of something whole, such as a fragment of a song. In the story, Toad's coach-house is in a terrible mess: it is «piled up to the roof—with fragments of motor-cars, none of them bigger than your hat!» Those pieces are small and broken, so fragments must mean broken bits.
explain: Look for clues in the words around the word. «None of them bigger than your hat» tells you the pieces are small. «Piled up to the roof» tells you there are a great many of them. Try your meaning in the sentence: «with small broken pieces of motor-cars» still makes sense, so you have found the right meaning.
explain: Fragment has a grammar meaning too. A sentence fragment is a group of words that is not a complete sentence. «Because it rained.» is a fragment: it has no main clause, so it leaves a question hanging. Add a main clause, such as «We stayed inside because it rained.», and the fragment becomes a complete sentence.
fact: A fragment is a small piece that has broken off something.
fact: A fragment can also be a small part of something, like a fragment of a conversation.
fact: «Fragments» means small broken pieces, as in «fragments of motor-cars» and «fragments of cold and leathery toast».
fact: A sentence fragment is not a complete sentence, because it has no main clause: «Because it rained.»
fact: To fragment means to break into small pieces, and scientists and archaeologists study fragments of pottery, rock and bone to learn about the past.
exercise: «Toad's coach-house is piled up to the roof with fragments of motor-cars, none of them bigger than your hat!» What are the fragments? | Big heavy engines | Tiny toy cars from a shop | *Small broken pieces of motor-cars | Whole new motor-cars
exercise: Which of these is a sentence fragment, not a complete sentence? | Toad ate his breakfast. | *Because it rained. | The egg-shells were on the floor. | The Mole went home early.
exercise: «Toad found a certain quantity of egg-shells, some fragments of cold and leathery toast, a coffee-pot three-fourths empty.» Find and copy one word that means broken pieces. | *fragments | breakfast | quantity | leathery
test: To fragment means to break into small pieces. Which word is closest in meaning? | Build | Sing | Sleep | *Break
test: What does a fragment of a song mean? | A song sung backwards | *A small part of the song | A whole song played loudly | A new song written today
exam: Which of these is a sentence fragment? | The egg-shells were on the floor. | *Fragments of cold toast. | Toad ate the cold toast. | Toad came down late.
